A||||3||86_Fastback||Headlight problem||||5
Z||000000||86_Fastback||11-25-1999||08:40 PM||||Yesterday my headlights stopped working.  They do not go up.  If I disconnect the blue wire and crank them up by hand, the headlights will go down when I hook up the blue wire.  I believe it is the isolation relay.  Am I right?  Does anyone know where the cheapest place to pick up a new one?  Thanks in advance for the help.<BR>-Gregg||||reg||5
Z||000001||ggarsk||11-26-1999||01:59 AM||||Headlights...next to the clutch system I think it is the biggest problem with our cars. On mine I got one headlight the goes up but not down. The other one goes down but not up. I know both motors are good. I think if I ever get them both to work I'll keel over in suprise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||dogtired||11-26-1999||03:26 AM||||Headlight Relays 2 weeks ago were $11.?? at AutoZone and $14.?? at ORilleys.<BR>Remember there are 3relays  in your system 1 on each headlight housing that have the same P/N and the one control just to the left of the left headlight on the inner fender well. and it has a different P/N they are not interchangable.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I just went through this same stuff with my 86GT and it turned out to be the controller relay. I HATE Relays.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Good luck, If you have fat fingers like me they will be all scratched up by the time you get it straightened out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>If you need the P/Ns? Yell back and I will go out and get them?||||reg||6
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||04:05 AM||||86_Fastback--go to <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/headlights.html</A> ||||reg||1
